<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore Oct retail sales up 1.1 percent on year.</title>
<headline>Singapore Oct retail sales up 1.1 percent on year.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's October retail sales index (base 1991) rose 1.1 percent compared to a year ago, the Department of Statistics said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>It was up marginally by 0.5 percent from September 1996.</p>
<p>Excluding motor vehicles, the index registered a month-on-month rise of 2.1 percent in October.</p>
<p>October retail sales were estimated at Singapore $1.98 billion. The statistics department said that year-on-year, in constant prices, the retail index rose by 2.1 percent.  </p>
<p>  Retail Sales Index (at Current Prices)   (pct change)</p>
<p>				   Month-on-Month     Yr-on-Yr</p>
<p>    Total index		    0.5		  1.1</p>
<p>    X-vehicle sales		2.1		  5.4</p>
<p>    Textiles/apparels	    2.7		  2.8</p>
<p>    Furniture/households	-5.2		  6.9</p>
<p>    Vehicle sales		 -4.2		-10.8</p>
<p>    Petrol stations		2.6		 10.0</p>
<p>    Departments/supermarts     6.2		 -1.8</p>
<p>    General provisions	   3.6		  2.6</p>
<p>    Other retail		   1.3		 15.2</p>
